Maya (Docs): Quick sync — I opened a docs PR that consolidates guidance for graceful fallback across 429s, timeouts, and context-limit behavior and migrates the SDK snippets into a unified examples section. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4123. Need eng + SDK review before merge. Main asks: confirm the runtime fallback ordering and that the JS/Python snippets show Retry-After + backoff handling. Holding for 48h :eyes:

Liam (Eng): Quick q: does the runtime prefer model-variant fallback or region fallback first? Also where do we call out honoring the `Retry-After` header vs recommending client backoff?

Maya (Docs): Runtime order in the PR draft is: 1) same-region compatible model variant, 2) lower-cost variant in the same model family, 3) cross-region fallback (only if customer routing allows). Text I'm proposing: 'When capacity constrained, Redwood will attempt model-variant fallbacks according to customer routing policy; if no compatible variant is available, requests may be routed to a compatible cross-region endpoint when permitted by policy.' Does that match reality?

Liam (Eng): Yes — please add a clear callout that Dedicated customers can pin model versions to avoid automatic fallback. Also SDK behavior: SDKs respect `Retry-After` when present. When header is absent, recommend exponential backoff with jitter, starting at ~200ms.

Noah (SDK): I'll update the SDK snippets. Draft JS snippet (will add to PR shortly):

```js
// pseudo-snippet showing 429 handling + Retry-After fallback
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
async function generateWithFallback(prompt) {
  try {
    return await client.generate({ model: 'redwood-1.0', input: prompt });
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.status === 429) {
      const retryAfter = parseInt(err.headers?.['retry-after'] || '0', 10);
      if (retryAfter > 0) await sleep(retryAfter * 1000);
      else await backoffWithJitter(200); // ms
      // attempt fallback model variant
      return await client.generate({ model: 'redwood-1.0-compact', input: prompt });
    }
    throw err;
  }
}
```

Noah (SDK): And a short Python example I'll add too (same pattern) and a concise `curl` example for ops: `curl -v -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -d '{"model":"redwood-1.0","input":"..."}' https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate` — server may return `Retry-After: 5` in headers.

Maya (Docs): Perfect. Can you also include a tiny helper for trimming long conversations (context window) — e.g., keep last N messages or trim tokens to 2048? Ops folks like explicit examples.

Noah (SDK): Added a small helper in the PR: `trimConversation(history, maxTokens = 2048)` — pseudo-code shows sliding-window trim. I'm linking the commit in the PR in ~30m.

Sophia (PM): Small ask: add a one-line note about canary rollouts: "canary routing may surface transient 429s; we recommend enabling automatic fallback during early rollouts." Also, can we include sample perf deltas (p99) from staging to show impact of fallback on latency? Even ballpark numbers help.

Maya (Docs): I don't have staging latency numbers. I'll add a TODO in the docs to paste p95/p99 numbers once infra provides them.

Liam (Eng): I'll pull p50/p95/p99 from staging and drop them into the PR by EOD.

DocsBot: Heads-up — the current 429 article has a stale internal link to `/old-retries`. Filed ticket: INFR-3421 to fix references.

Maya (Docs): Thanks — I updated the broken link references in the draft and left a note at the top of the file: `<!-- TODO: insert staging perf numbers (Liam) -->`. Plan: merge after 48h if no blocking comments. Tagging @Noah (SDK) for snippet review and @Liam (Eng) for numbers. :shipit:
